SWEET nav11 (patch 0255, T-c87c, G-10b-nav; input injection + log only): witness and one input fix for the rep-0 Settings desync left by T-bf77. (1) Witness: `SWEET EXEC: NAME t NS swaps N` after every exec line (kern_exec.c, same clock as `SWEET NAV: ... now` and `SWEET SWAPT: now`) and `SWEET NAV: EVT t NS down|up X,Y act IDX rep R swaps N pref_exec C` per HID touch edge, so the touch that precedes the `exec Preferences` of the stalled boots is named to the millisecond (nav8/9/10 [obs docs/reviews/T-c87c-proof.md s1]: Preferences exec 7-9 s after the first unlock swipe with the wake tap at 540,1200 and at 540,70 alike, SpringBoard and backboardd CPU react to every swipe so the input is not delivered late at that level). (2) Fix: when Preferences exec'd inside the unlock window (count read at the first attempt vs after the swap-verified retries) the unlock row ends with the calibrated app-home swipe (540,2398 -> 1800 -> 1200, 2 s settle) before rep 0 goes on, so settings-open / general-open / about-open start from the home screen as in nav3/nav5. Logs `SWEET NAV: unlock: Preferences launched inside the unlock window ...` and `... app-home swipe done ...`; the unlock window line now carries the exec counts and the home swipe state. No register, no store to hardware.
